{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>May YHWH appoint.</b> Since Moses heard the Omnipresent say to him, 'Give the inheritance of Zelophehad to his daughters,' he said: The hour has come that I should demand my need — that my sons inherit my greatness. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: Not so did it arise in thought before Me. Joshua is worthy to receive the reward of his attendance, that he never departed from within the tent (Exodus 33:11) — and this is what Solomon said (Proverbs 27): 'He who tends the fig tree eats its fruit' (Tanchuma)." "<b>Elohei ha-ruchot.</b> Why is this said? He said before Him: Master of the universe, the disposition of each and every one is revealed before You, and no two are alike. Appoint over them a leader who will bear each and every one according to his disposition (Yalkut Shimoni)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:03.977596241Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}